# Database migrations

- Whenever a change adds or modifies database-backed schema, permissions, roles, seed data, or required persisted values, include the corresponding migration in the same change.
- Add migrations to the correct migration system and update its metadata or journal when required.
- Ensure the migration works both for existing deployments and clean environments.
- Do not treat runtime defaults, application constants, or seed scripts as substitutes for a deployable migration.
- Tenant databases are migrated fleet-wide while each tenant instance runs its own pinned
  application version, so a migration must not break the version already deployed. Never add a
  `NOT NULL` column without a way for the database to fill it on its own (`DEFAULT`, `SERIAL`, or a
  `BEFORE INSERT` trigger): an older instance omits the column and its inserts fail with 23502.
